280
00:11:58,039 --> 00:11:58,440
Sure.

281
00:11:58,440 --> 00:11:59,080
Sure, come on.

282
00:11:59,080 --> 00:12:00,559
Come on.

283
00:12:00,559 --> 00:12:01,679
Give me a V.

284
00:12:01,679 --> 00:12:04,360
V.

285
00:12:04,360 --> 00:12:05,279
So gorgeous.

286
00:12:05,279 --> 00:12:06,840
Not bad, kids.

287
00:12:06,840 --> 00:12:08,320
Basketball Club and Drama Club, get ready.

288
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:09,440
You're next.

289
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:10,759
Come on!

290
00:12:10,759 --> 00:12:11,320
Okay.

291
00:12:11,320 --> 00:12:11,559
Come on!

292
00:12:11,559 --> 00:12:13,000
Thank you, Mr. Wang. Come on!

293
00:12:15,039 --> 00:12:16,759
Seniors, have you memorized the lines?

294
00:12:17,519 --> 00:12:18,440
Just a few lines.

295
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:19,519
I've memorized them long ago.

296
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:20,960
You can just look forward to

297
00:12:20,960 --> 00:12:22,000
my wonderful performance

298
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:23,279
today.

299
00:12:24,240 --> 00:12:25,200
The next program

300
00:12:25,200 --> 00:12:26,960
is a creative stage play

301
00:12:26,960 --> 00:12:28,480
brought by the Drama Club and the Basketball Club,

302
00:12:28,480 --> 00:12:29,360
The Thorn Prince.

303
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:30,399
My son is coming.

304
00:12:30,840 --> 00:12:31,919
The sons are coming.

305
00:12:32,639 --> 00:12:33,080
Take good pictures.

306
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:34,000
It's up to you.

307
00:12:34,440 --> 00:12:35,159
Of course.

308
00:12:35,360 --> 00:12:36,000
Come on.

309
00:12:38,399 --> 00:12:39,720
I heard that the leading actor of this show

310
00:12:39,720 --> 00:12:41,000
is Li Haoyu.

311
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:41,559
Yeah.

312
00:12:41,559 --> 00:12:43,120
I heard that they've been rehearsing for a long time.

313
00:12:47,159 --> 00:12:50,120
Your Highness.

314
00:12:51,120 --> 00:12:52,080
Your Highness.

315
00:12:53,320 --> 00:12:54,919
Stop messing around.

316
00:12:55,480 --> 00:12:57,440
Your ball is about to start.

317
00:12:57,639 --> 00:12:59,120
What ball?

318
00:12:59,519 --> 00:13:01,080
I'm not going to take part in it.

319
00:13:01,080 --> 00:13:02,840
This is your coming-of-age ball.

320
00:13:03,879 --> 00:13:04,559
Come on.

321
00:13:07,480 --> 00:13:08,440
Prince.

322
00:13:10,039 --> 00:13:10,879
Your Majesty.

323
00:13:10,879 --> 00:13:11,799
Royal Father.

324
00:13:14,200 --> 00:13:14,960
Prince.

325
00:13:15,720 --> 00:13:17,559
If you keep making trouble like this,

326
00:13:17,799 --> 00:13:19,799
I will no longer satisfy

327
00:13:19,799 --> 00:13:21,320
any of your demands.

328
00:13:25,519 --> 00:13:26,320
You fool,

329
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:28,279
what are you waiting for?

330
00:13:28,679 --> 00:13:30,639
Put the crown on me!

331
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:34,039
Why am I always the one who gets hurt?

332
00:13:35,919 --> 00:13:37,440
He's a pretty good prince.

333
00:13:37,440 --> 00:13:38,440
Yeah, yeah.

334
00:13:38,919 --> 00:13:40,720
He's got a knack for acting.

335
00:13:50,440 --> 00:13:52,879
These are the same gifts every year.

336
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:56,480
Celebrating with you lot

337
00:13:56,960 --> 00:13:58,720
is such a waste of time.

338
00:14:00,200 --> 00:14:01,960
Get out! All of you!

339
00:14:04,200 --> 00:14:05,200
How dare you!

340
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:08,000
Your Highness

341
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:10,559
Your Highness

342
00:14:10,559 --> 00:14:12,159
Your best friend is here.

343
00:14:12,399 --> 00:14:13,440
The Dala Knight has arrived.

344
00:14:15,279 --> 00:14:16,240
Bring him up.

345
00:14:18,279 --> 00:14:20,480
Welcome the Dala Knight.

346
00:14:20,480 --> 00:14:21,039
Come on.

347
00:14:27,879 --> 00:14:28,759
Your Majesty

348
00:14:29,720 --> 00:14:30,559
Your Highness.

349
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:32,720
Dala Knight.

350
00:14:33,240 --> 00:14:34,279
What birthday gift

351
00:14:34,279 --> 00:14:34,840
have you prepared

352
00:14:34,840 --> 00:14:35,960
for me this time?

353
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:37,480
Sorry, Your Highness.

354
00:14:38,039 --> 00:14:39,639
I didn't prepare a gift for you.

355
00:14:40,120 --> 00:14:41,279
What's going on?

356
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:42,919
How come there's no gift?

357
00:14:44,519 --> 00:14:45,679
The script is well written.

358
00:14:45,679 --> 00:14:46,639
Keep it up, Shuang.

359
00:14:46,639 --> 00:14:47,639
Keep an eye on him.

360
00:14:47,639 --> 00:14:48,440
Okay, Mr. Wang.

361
00:14:49,639 --> 00:14:50,639
Your Highness

362
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:52,960
I saw everything

363
00:14:52,960 --> 00:14:54,200
you did just now.

364
00:14:54,759 --> 00:14:56,240
I don't want to be friends

365
00:14:56,240 --> 00:14:57,919
with a rude person like you.

366
00:14:58,200 --> 00:14:58,600
So

367
00:14:59,240 --> 00:15:00,399
I won't go to

368
00:15:00,759 --> 00:15:01,919
tonight's ball.

369
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:02,960
Goodbye.

370
00:15:07,559 --> 00:15:08,720
Goodbye.

371
00:15:11,320 --> 00:15:12,080
What?

372
00:15:12,279 --> 00:15:13,080
Why did they all leave?

373
00:15:13,399 --> 00:15:14,120
What's going on?

374
00:15:21,519 --> 00:15:22,720
My child.

375
00:15:23,600 --> 00:15:24,559
I'm

376
00:15:25,200 --> 00:15:27,320
so disappointed in you.

377
00:15:35,919 --> 00:15:36,919
Prince.

378
00:15:36,919 --> 00:15:39,159
Please be alone for a while.

379
00:15:50,840 --> 00:15:51,440
Help!

380
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:54,080
Why is it different from the script?

381
00:15:54,399 --> 00:15:56,559
What should I do now?

382
00:15:57,720 --> 00:15:59,440
Is this Li Haoyu's monologue?

383
00:15:59,720 --> 00:16:01,440
Why is he alone?

384
00:16:04,080 --> 00:16:05,440
Is this part of the design?

385
00:16:06,559 --> 00:16:08,639
Maybe, let's see.

386
00:16:09,080 --> 00:16:10,480
Did he forget his lines?

387
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:14,000
What's going on?

388
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:15,240
What was Li Haoyu doing?

389
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,320
When he was on stage,

390
00:16:23,759 --> 00:16:24,919
he held my hand.

391
00:16:25,639 --> 00:16:27,159
I could tell

392
00:16:27,679 --> 00:16:29,519
he didn't know what was going on.

393
00:16:31,759 --> 00:16:32,759
Could it be

394
00:16:32,759 --> 00:16:34,080
that he really forgot his lines?

395
00:16:36,360 --> 00:16:37,120
It's all my fault.

396
00:16:38,919 --> 00:16:40,440
I insisted on changing the script at the last minute.

397
00:16:41,879 --> 00:16:42,799
Is it possible

398
00:16:42,799 --> 00:16:44,840
that he hasn't even seen it?

399
00:16:45,639 --> 00:16:47,000
Is it possible

400
00:16:47,240 --> 00:16:49,000
he didn't know there was a new script?

401
00:16:57,759 --> 00:16:59,320
[The final script has been sent.]

402
00:16:59,320 --> 00:17:00,399
[Please check it.]

403
00:17:02,799 --> 00:17:04,559
[Got it. Thanks.]

404
00:17:04,559 --> 00:17:05,079
[Everyone,]

405
00:17:05,079 --> 00:17:06,279
[make sure to memorize the new lines before bed.]

406
00:17:06,880 --> 00:17:08,200
[Got it. Thanks.]

407
00:17:08,400 --> 00:17:09,960
[Got it. Thanks, President.]

408
00:17:28,960 --> 00:17:29,400
What are you doing?

409
00:17:29,400 --> 00:17:30,240
What are you doing?

410
00:17:39,160 --> 00:17:39,920
Gu Chenyang,

411
00:17:40,359 --> 00:17:41,599
What are you doing with the microphone?

412
00:17:43,039 --> 00:17:44,319
Help him finish this act.

413
00:18:14,880 --> 00:18:16,039
Thorn Prince,

414
00:18:16,799 --> 00:18:19,480
now everyone has left you.

415
00:18:19,799 --> 00:18:20,640
How do you feel?

416
00:18:21,559 --> 00:18:22,240
Who?

417
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:24,079
Who is speaking?

418
00:18:24,480 --> 00:18:26,400
I am your inner demon.

419
00:18:35,519 --> 00:18:37,599
I have everything I want.

420
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:39,799
I can do whatever I want.

421
00:18:40,759 --> 00:18:42,680
How could there be an inner demon?

422
00:18:43,759 --> 00:18:45,240
Then why didn't you

423
00:18:45,240 --> 00:18:46,200
like the gold and silver

424
00:18:46,200 --> 00:18:47,680
of the princes

425
00:18:48,279 --> 00:18:48,960
but only wanted

426
00:18:48,960 --> 00:18:50,720
the gift of Dala Knight?

427
00:18:52,799 --> 00:18:53,920
That's because

428
00:18:54,960 --> 00:18:57,039
Dala Knight is my good friend.

429
00:18:58,160 --> 00:18:59,599
You need a friend.

430
00:19:08,319 --> 00:19:10,039
They're good at turning the tables.

431
00:19:10,039 --> 00:19:10,839
Yeah.

432
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:11,880
I...

433
00:19:13,240 --> 00:19:14,400
I don't need it.

434
00:19:15,359 --> 00:19:16,160
I can live freely

435
00:19:16,160 --> 00:19:17,440
on my own.

436
00:19:17,839 --> 00:19:19,480
Are you

437
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,079
free now?

438
00:19:24,599 --> 00:19:26,480
You always pretend to be unconcerned,

439
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:29,960
putting up thorns to reject the whole world,

440
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:32,240
thinking that

441
00:19:32,240 --> 00:19:33,720
you won't get hurt.

442
00:19:35,200 --> 00:19:36,039
I don't.

443
00:19:37,400 --> 00:19:38,519
You still think

444
00:19:39,160 --> 00:19:40,960
everyone will leave you in the end.

445
00:19:41,599 --> 00:19:43,359
The only one you can rely on

446
00:19:43,359 --> 00:19:44,720
is yourself.

447
00:19:45,880 --> 00:19:46,799
Am I wrong?

448
00:19:47,839 --> 00:19:49,400
As long as I am strong enough,

449
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:51,319
I don't need anyone.

450
00:19:56,279 --> 00:19:57,599
Now,

451
00:19:58,279 --> 00:19:59,519
do you still think so?

452
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:19,799
Although

453
00:20:20,279 --> 00:20:22,000
I didn't write a single line of dialogue,

454
00:20:22,359 --> 00:20:24,759
I still feel so touched.

455
00:20:26,079 --> 00:20:27,359
The seniors are so amazing.

456
00:20:30,200 --> 00:20:31,000
Answer me.

457
00:20:31,559 --> 00:20:33,000
Do you still think so now?

458
00:20:38,960 --> 00:20:39,960
In the universe,

459
00:20:41,079 --> 00:20:42,640
I like pulsars the most.

460
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:45,039
Pulsar

461
00:20:47,319 --> 00:20:48,160
is a star

462
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:49,680
that looks very cool,

463
00:20:51,720 --> 00:20:52,839
But actually,

464
00:20:54,440 --> 00:20:56,440
they are very desolate

465
00:20:57,079 --> 00:20:58,079
and lonely.

466
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:00,440
Because there are no other stars

467
00:21:00,440 --> 00:21:01,559
that can get close.

468
00:21:03,039 --> 00:21:04,400
For a long time,

469
00:21:05,880 --> 00:21:07,400
I was such a star.

470
00:21:09,319 --> 00:21:10,240
But

471
00:21:11,240 --> 00:21:12,599
it's not that I can't be approached,

472
00:21:14,960 --> 00:21:16,160
it's that I

473
00:21:16,160 --> 00:21:17,799
actively distanced myself from the star clusters.

474
00:21:19,720 --> 00:21:21,039
I was afraid to be approached,

475
00:21:22,839 --> 00:21:24,200
and afraid to be abandoned,

476
00:21:25,960 --> 00:21:27,279
so I chose

477
00:21:28,279 --> 00:21:29,680
to abandon the universe.

478
00:21:41,920 --> 00:21:42,960
But now,

479
00:21:43,839 --> 00:21:45,279
everything has changed.

480
00:22:09,759 --> 00:22:10,519
Now,

481
00:22:11,240 --> 00:22:11,920
I have found

482
00:22:11,920 --> 00:22:13,319
my partner.

483
00:22:16,720 --> 00:22:17,640
The pulsar

484
00:22:18,400 --> 00:22:19,720
is no longer lonely,

485
00:22:21,359 --> 00:22:21,880
but us

486
00:22:21,880 --> 00:22:23,200
shining together.

487
00:22:32,960 --> 00:22:34,559
As long as we are together,

488
00:22:35,119 --> 00:22:36,960
we can rock the universe.

489
00:24:55,640 --> 00:24:56,960
They are so excellent.

490
00:24:56,960 --> 00:24:58,039
Yeah.

491
00:24:58,039 --> 00:24:59,640
I really admire them.

492
00:24:59,640 --> 00:25:01,000
I'm so proud.

493
00:26:03,519 --> 00:26:04,440
Next,

494
00:26:04,440 --> 00:26:05,680
let me introduce

495
00:26:05,680 --> 00:26:06,480
our band,

496
00:26:06,480 --> 00:26:07,720
Pulsar Band.

497
00:26:10,759 --> 00:26:13,079
Keyboard, Gu Chenyang.

498
00:26:15,119 --> 00:26:17,119
Bass, Lin Qingyuan.

499
00:26:17,680 --> 00:26:18,799
Thank you.

500
00:26:19,200 --> 00:26:21,200
Guitar, Zhou Yang.

501
00:26:23,400 --> 00:26:25,720
Drummer, Li Haoyu.

502
00:26:29,240 --> 00:26:30,480
And our guest,

503
00:26:30,480 --> 00:26:31,279
violin,

504
00:26:31,279 --> 00:26:32,880
Fu Binyan.

505
00:26:34,599 --> 00:26:36,519
And our script writer,

506
00:26:36,519 --> 00:26:38,440
Chen Song.

507
00:26:43,599 --> 00:26:44,200
Go.

508
00:26:51,519 --> 00:26:52,400
Thank you all for coming to see

509
00:26:52,400 --> 00:26:53,480
our performance this time.

510
00:26:54,359 --> 00:26:54,799
Now,

511
00:26:55,480 --> 00:26:56,400
let's shout out

512
00:26:56,400 --> 00:26:57,240
our name again.

513
00:26:58,039 --> 00:26:58,720
We are

514
00:26:59,279 --> 00:27:01,960
Pulsar Band.

515
00:27:03,319 --> 00:27:13,079
Pulsar Band.
